t@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e2e6188eb5714c19d2847884c2d18f6f83a8eea58b7f09868902e4d1a54aa65f","event_uuid":"b1f787b2-367e-46a4-91b6-2b28da95277e","position":{"commit_sha":"c75be9e1b439735b60187e18d26a8a3f2734542b","position":"1786729551615777001-b1f787b2-367e-46a4-91b6-2b28da95277e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"40ebaea0da2c97d952c17d4c19bd8f6e4610c13b1b79e545e49d91dba91cfcff","event_uuid":"3a998e3f-4456-4fbd-bfd1-a816ae546055","position":{"commit_sha":"4b0bee2f76213fe00665d4c27928b5895bf18b85","position":"1786729556414586001-3a998e3f-4456-4fbd-bfd1-a816ae546055"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786694355830665001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"deda412d-c4b9-4ebb-ab1c-f01319fbb75e","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3211-be4f-d4aa-4b5c"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nFollow-up (fix b) to creatable-foldable-arthropods (fix a, merged a0fc8d43556 / Gerrit 1761). A second, independent defect remains in the verifier's evidence-banking path: at SEARCH EXHAUSTION, `BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE` banks `met=false` — i.e. \"the criterion is unmet\" — when what the run actually established is only \"the search budget ran out before sufficient evidence was found\". This misattributes absence-of-evidence as evidence-of-absence, producing false FAIL verdicts on tickets whose evidence exists but was not reached within the window.\n\n## Proposed fix\nDistinguish THREE evidence outcomes: met, refuted, and insufficient (search exhausted without a determination) — the third carried as a framework-set `evidence_sufficient:false` marker riding alongside `met:false`, per the verdict_obtainable precedent (completion.py:516; schema :14-18), so verdict/met vocabularies and every fail-closed consumer stay unchanged. The insufficiency marker must originate in the banking WRITE path, whose chokepoints are bool-typed today:\n- `CompletionEvidencePolicy.fallback_record` (completion_tool_policy.py:100-101) passes a literal `False` through the record tool — at exhaustion it must bank `met=false` PLUS the `evidence_sufficient:false` marker, via an internal write path (not the model-facing tool).\n- `CriterionBank.upsert` (completion_banking.py:441-461) — persist the optional marker alongside the bool `met` (the \"writes remain bool-only\" docstring contract updates with it).\n- `record_criterion_verdict`'s model-facing tool signature (:539) stays BOOL — the marker is exclusively the policy-side exhaustion outcome, never a model-tool input.\n- `harvest_structured_into_bank` (:583) keeps its bool gate but must carry the marker through re-harvest instead of dropping it.\n\n**Full consumer graph (all bool-coercing/validating sites change together):**\n- **Schema (`src/rebar/schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json`)**: follow the `verdict_obtainable` precedent (schema :14-18, completion.py:516) — a framework-set boolean marker riding ALONGSIDE {PASS, FAIL}, not a third token, keeping the normalizing fail-safe and every consumer's blocking behavior unchanged. Same pattern: `verdict` stays PASS/FAIL (insufficient evidence still FAILs and blocks), `met` stays bool, and two OPTIONAL framework-set markers are added: `criteria[].evidence_sufficient:false` (this false is exhaustion, not refutation) and top-level `evidence_sufficient:false` (present iff no criterion is genuinely unmet but ≥1 is insufficient). Consumers reading only verdict/met are untouched; message-rendering consumers read the marker. Both rendering seams validate against this schema (completion_recovery.py:674, :774).\n- **`_validate_coverage` (completion_recovery.py:364-368, run at :717)**: met stays bool → type gate and :370 PASS cross-check unchanged; markers must survive validation untouched.\n- **`_run_finalizer` (completion_recovery.py:741)**: the banked-evidence payload must carry the marker so the LLM finalizer sees exhaustion, not refutation.\n- **Unbanked/exhausted placeholder branches** (`assemble_deterministic_verdict` :646-660, `merge_finalizer_with_bank` :715+): a never-banked criterion at exhaustion IS absence-of-evidence — placeholders carry the marker (keeping `exhausted`) instead of a bare `met:false` + high-severity FAIL finding.\n- **`reconcile_verdict` (completion.py:495-564)**: the `:522` PASS/FAIL normalization is UNTOUCHED. Changes: preserve the framework-set markers through reconciliation, and make the `:564` remediation branch marker-aware — a FAIL carrying `evidence_sufficient:false` gets insufficient-evidence remediation (re-verify / widen scope / operator-attest) instead of unmet-criteria guidance. The `:526` verdict_obtainable fault path is unaffected: insufficient-evidence criteria still emit findings, so the no-findings heuristic never sees them.\n- **Close-gate refusal (close_precheck.py:571-589)**: still gates on non-PASS (unchanged, fail-closed) — but when the verdict carries `evidence_sufficient:false` it reports \"insufficient evidence\" + the marker's remediation instead of asserting \"N unmet criteria\".\n- **Finalizer prompt (src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier_finalizer.md:23-28)**: currently collapses missing/truncated evidence into `met:false` + high-severity finding + FAIL — the defect at the LLM seam. Update the decision rule: banked insufficient entries echo as `met:false`, findings text says insufficient; the framework re-stamps the marker post-merge (the stamp is the enforcement, the prompt aligns the text).\n- **Completion sidecar (`completion_sidecar.py:335`)**: persists `criteria` as-is — verified pass-through; a round-trip test pins it, no code change expected.\n- **Banked-entry rendering** in `assemble_deterministic_verdict` (:619-640) and `merge_finalizer_with_bank` (:705-714): marker-carrying entries emit `met:false + evidence_sufficient:false` with an insufficient-evidence finding, not a bare unmet-criterion FAIL finding. The change is honesty of message and recorded class, never gate leniency.\n\n## Scope\n- The banking WRITE path: `fallback_record` wiring in src/rebar/llm/completion_tool_policy.py (exhaustion site), and in src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py: `CriterionBank.upsert` (persists the marker), `record_criterion_verdict` (unchanged bool tool signature — guard only), `harvest_structured_into_bank` (markers survive re-harvest), and BOTH unbanked/exhausted placeholder branches (assemble_deterministic_verdict :646-660, merge_finalizer_with_bank :715+).\n- src/rebar/schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json — optional framework-set `evidence_sufficient:false` markers (top-level + per-criterion), verdict_obtainable pattern; verdict vocabulary unchanged.\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py — `_validate_coverage` markers survive validation; `_run_finalizer` payload carries the marker (:741).\n- src/rebar/llm/completion.py — `reconcile_verdict` preserves the evidence_sufficient markers; :564 remediation branch marker-aware.\n- src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py — refusal message keys on the marker (insufficient evidence vs unmet criteria); still refuses both.\n- src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier_finalizer.md — evidence-sufficiency decision rule (:23-28).\n- src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py — verified pass-through (round-trip test only; no code change expected).\n- Tests: exhaustion banks the marker; genuine refutation stays bare met=false; rendering distinguishes the two.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] At search exhaustion, banked fallback evidence carries `evidence_sufficient:false` (never a bare `met=false`); new unit test.\n- [ ] A marker-carrying bank entry survives `harvest_structured_into_bank` round-trips; the model-facing `record_criterion_verdict` tool signature remains bool-only; unit tests.\n- [ ] A genuine positive refutation still banks `met=false` and still yields FAIL; checked by a guard test.\n- [ ] BOTH rendering seams — `assemble_deterministic_verdict` and `merge_finalizer_with_bank` — emit `met:false + evidence_sufficient:false` for insufficient-evidence entries, INCLUDING their unbanked/exhausted placeholder branches; per-seam and per-branch rendering tests.\n- [ ] Schema validates marker-carrying AND existing all-bool records; `_validate_coverage` passes markers through, still rejects untyped records; `_run_finalizer` payload carries the marker; sidecar round-trip preserves it; unit tests each.\n- [ ] Close gate still BLOCKS on insufficient evidence (verdict stays FAIL) but the refusal reports insufficient evidence + remediation, not unmet criteria; `reconcile_verdict` preserves markers + swaps remediation; gate + reconcile tests.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) before close.\n\n## Out of scope\nGuard/memo interaction (fix a, landed); retry policy; prompt changes OTHER than the finalizer's evidence-sufficiency rule above.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion_tool_policy.py","reason":"fallback_record banks met=false + evidence_sufficient:false marker at exhaustion"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py","reason":"upsert persists marker; harvest carries it; both rendering seams incl unbanked placeholder branches"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py","reason":"markers survive _validate_coverage; _run_finalizer payload carries marker"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion.py","reason":"reconcile_verdict preserves markers; remediation branch marker-aware"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","reason":"refusal keys on marker: insufficient evidence vs unmet criteria"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json","reason":"optional framework-set evidence_sufficient markers, verdict_obtainable pattern"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier_finalizer.md","reason":"evidence-sufficiency decision rule"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_completion_tool_policy.py","reason":"exhaustion banks marker; genuine refutation stays bare met=false"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_completion_evidence_tristate.py","reason":"new: per-seam rendering, schema, harvest round-trip, reconcile + gate behavior"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ec51dc60-b32e-49cc-9c63-2cde5ec83d69","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1d71-a76c-04f6-4642","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion verifier banks met=false at search exhaustion — should bank insufficient_evidence (tri-state)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d25bf152-2ba0-4afb-be73-7db7044031a4","ec51dc60-b32e-49cc-9c63-2cde5ec83d69","d03bc8d0-2d36-4b2a-815a-805b5e9e52fb","7d18bb71-b102-451e-85c4-56349ee32015","a5e79e05-0a96-4c47-99de-39f711c8b377","1cf55390-cc44-4fcf-89b3-0ed4a9566317","623dbde0-16bc-4473-a206-9079b6221cdd","f2aaabc5-9b6d-4b1c-ba89-4ac8a525987b","790efd11-3319-4393-b19b-ce9e503aa8ac","2a6b0a85-75de-41b8-b2c9-7812983984f6","cb3363ca-9fc4-47c5-92df-fc2a7d2a5b01","b1f787b2-367e-46a4-91b6-2b28da95277e","3a998e3f-4456-4fbd-bfd1-a816ae546055"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":17867295564145